DIR - list a directory››Syntax:› DIR [+|-][A|H|P|S] [d:][path][name]›     [/A|C|L|P|W]› DIRS [+|-][A|H|P|S] [d:][path][name]›     [/A|C|P]››DIR shows name, extension, size in›bytes (k for KiB above 999999), date›and time; <DIR> marks a directory. The›volume and directory names come first,›free sectors last. No name means *.*.›A directory name must end in > or \ to›list its contents.››DIRS gives the short Atari DOS style›list: sizes in sectors, * before›protected entries.››Attributes select what is listed: A›archived, H hidden, P protected, S›directory. The default is -H; DIR +›lists everything.››Switches:› /A  show the attributes› /C  count the entries› /L  show symlink targets› /P  wait for a key every screen› /W  names only, in columns››Examples:› DIR *.COM› DIR + /A› DIRS D2:>GAMES>››See also: ATR, FIND›